{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["Why do you show yourselves — like ״לכה ונתראה פנים״, Amatziah who saw fit to show his greatness to Yoash king of Israel; so too here: why do you show yourselves before the people as though you have all the grain you need, when you are lingering here without grain and all the people are going down to Egypt to buy grain, while you sit and make a show as though you have?"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {0 "The allusion is to 2 Kings 14:8; Rashbam writes the phrase פנים דאמציה as part of his running sentence without separating it as a lemma, so it is left integrated."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:04.433323234Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}